                <pb facs="0508" n="504" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg504"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/12975: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bucknell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-07T11:00:00+01:00">May 7, 1938—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 7—9:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>79. Secretary General has received a note from Chinese permanent delegate
                    bringing up the nature of Japanese outrages in Sino-Japanese conflict. Hoo asks
                    that this be circulated to members of the League and to members of the Far
                    Eastern Advisory Committee.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucknell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
